fter": -3.79, "points_lost": 0.03, "best": "C3"}, {"turn": 63, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -3.79, "lead_after": -4.0, "points_lost": 0.21, "best": "G3"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Sixteen-point swings around the J9 ko", "summary": "Opus 5.5 won as White by 4 points. Black built a lead of +16.1 by move 32, then gave it away at move 35 (E9, 20.8 points lost). After that, the top-right corner turned into a ko where the lead swung by about 16 points several times. Opus 5.5 played the last decisive J9 and held the win; both sides averaged about 3 points lost per move (3.2 and 3.3).", "moments": [{"turn": 35, "text": "The 12k, with a lead of +12.5, played E9 at the top. The engine wanted J7, and E9 dropped the lead to -8.3, a loss of 20.8 points. This was the worst move of the game."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with J7, but the engine's choice was H9. The move lost 20.8 points and put Black's lead back from -8.3 to +12.5. A 20.8-point blunder met a 20.8-point blunder."}, {"turn": 39, "text": "Black's J6 lost 17.0 points, taking the lead from +12.4 to -4.6. The engine's choice was J9. That corner point kept deciding the game from here on."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "With the ko at J9 on the board, Opus 5.5 played F6 instead of the engine's G6. It lost 17.2 points, and Black's lead went from -4.8 to +12.4. The very next move, Black's G6, lost 16.4 right back."}, {"turn": 52, "text": "This J9 matches the engine's choice and cost only -0.1 points. By then Black stood at -3.9, and the position stayed near -4.0 until the two passes, which fits the final W+4."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py, shown in the second listing, only parses the pasted board and does a flood fill to print each group's stones and liberties, flagging groups with 2 or fewer liberties. It looks at the current position, scores no candidate moves and plays nothing forward, so it is a helper.", "stop": false}}